From: Wine upstream contributors (see commit list)
Subject: [PATCH] Carry WineHQ fixes for macOS-specific behaviour.

Twelve WineHQ commits from wine-11.2 to wine-11.17, applied unchanged in
upstream order; test-only hunks are omitted. They are the first batch
carried under the macOS-fix rule in CLAUDE.md section 3: each fixes a
defect present in the pinned base, touches only Wine code that CrossOver
keeps unchanged, and changes no protocol or shared structure. d56f36c1aa
also changes win32u and winex11 code that macOS does not reach; it was
approved individually and is carried unchanged. See
docs/upstream-reviews.md, "macOS fix batch 1".

  98a370e5e1 (wine-11.2, Tim Clem): ntdll: Report free space for "important" data on macOS.
  7d29860d06 (wine-11.3, Rémi Bernon): winemac: Register clipboard format with NtUserRegisterWindowMessage.
  92df8e37e5 (wine-11.3, Esme Povirk): gdiplus: Remove an assumption that an enum type is unsigned.
  4f1ecabee9 (wine-11.5, Marc-Aurel Zent): winemac: Avoid matching scan code 0 in GetKeyNameText.
  3b1ab64042 (wine-11.6, Rémi Bernon): winemac: Keep current user locale in the generated HKLs.
  c8b7150680 (wine-11.7, Tim Clem): ntdll: Fall back to statfs if "important" free space is 0 on macOS.
  1bfb493cd0 (wine-11.7, Tim Clem): winemac.drv: Handle windows becoming invalid between WM_QUERYENDSESSION and WM_ENDSESSION.
  d56f36c1aa (wine-11.8, Zhiyi Zhang): Revert "win32u: Don't forcefully activate windows before restoring them.".
  d14d0b22b4 (wine-11.10, Marc-Aurel Zent): winemac: Set IME open status depending on HKL.
  eefbbc07a8 (wine-11.10, Feifan He): winemac: Handle reset parameter in ClipCursor.
  1a1d1f3f38 (wine-11.16, Zhiyi Zhang): winemac.drv: Hide client_view when flushing window surfaces.
  53a91cdcbe (wine-11.17, Brendan Shanks): winemac: Fix memory leak in get_format_entries().

